--- Technical ---
### Changed

- Integrate the M9 Frontend Redesign into `main` and add v1.9.0 release notes. ([#244](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/244))

### Added

- Add inline citation badges to sanitized assistant Markdown through `AssistantMarkdown.Render(markdown, citations)`, retaining unmatched citations in the sources list. ([#245](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/245))
- Make the first actionable `SuggestedNextSteps` item a primary ticket action, with remaining steps in an overflow menu. ([#237](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/237))
- Add a keyboard-operated `CommandPalette` for navigation and ticket search, opened with `Ctrl/Cmd+K`. ([#236](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/236))
- Update ticket status optimistically on the board and detail view, restoring the previous state when a change is rejected. ([#235](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/235))
- Replace ticket status and assignee dialogs with inline `MudMenu` popovers. ([#234](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/234))
- Add inline assistant citation badges with hover and keyboard-focus previews, retaining unanchored citations in the sources list. ([#233](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/233))
- Include the active agent roster in the chat system prompt using `GetAgentsHandler`. ([#221](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/221))
- Force one `check_grounding` call through `tool_choice` after retrieval when no grounding check has run. ([#218](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/218))
- Centralize palette, spacing, radius, elevation, and semantic chip colors in `Theme/DesignTokens.cs`. ([#213](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/213))

### Fixed

- Wrap board card titles in `board-card__title-row` so the two-line clamp applies. ([#240](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/240))
- Fix the assistant composer panel styling with `::deep .assistant-chat` so its send button stays inside the panel. ([#239](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/239))
- Fix the ticket queue `Category` header width and styling so it no longer overlaps `Due`. ([#238](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/238))
- Require the chat system prompt to confirm writes only after successful tool results and avoid re-asking for changes the user already requested. ([#223](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/223))
- Render ticket summary timestamps in `Anthropic:UserTimeZone` through `BuildTicketPrompt`. ([#222](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/222))
- Report technical `search_knowledge_base` failures with `IsError: true` while keeping the unavailable result distinct. ([#220](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/220))
- Score grounding by sentence-to-passage semantic similarity in `SemanticGroundingEvaluator`, with `LexicalGroundingEvaluator` as the fallback. ([#219](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/219))
